<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Kiosk offline (Critical)">
        <FluentText>
            A kiosk stopped responding, or was shut down and hasn't come back, for long enough to count as down. It's only
            raised during the location's opening hours, and clears when the kiosk is back online.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Kiosk needs attention (Warning)">
        <FluentText>
            A kiosk has reported a problem for at least 10 minutes during opening hours, such as low disk space, high
            CPU or memory, or its DMX lighting device not open. The alert lists the problems. It clears once the kiosk
            reports itself healthy.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Missed clock-in (Warning)">
        <FluentText>
            A published shift has been running for the <strong>Missed clock-in alert after</strong> time in Rota settings
            (15 minutes to start with) and the person on it hasn't clocked in at that location. It clears when they clock in,
            or when the shift is removed, unpublished or given to someone else. If the shift ends with nobody clocked in, the
            alert stays open for you to deal with, and the shift shows as missed on Timesheets.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Training overdue (Warning)">
        <FluentText>
            Someone's training is past its due date. It clears when they complete it, or the course is no longer assigned to
            them. Compliance lists everyone who is behind.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Document expiring (Info) and Document expired (Warning)">
        <FluentText>
            A staff document has reached the reminder date set when it was uploaded, or its expiry date has passed. The same
            alert moves from Info to Warning when it expires. It clears when a renewed document is uploaded or the old one is
            removed. Documents don't belong to a location, so the alert goes to the location the person works at.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Automation rule failed (Warning)">
        <FluentText>
            An automation rule ran but at least one of its actions failed. The alert shows the first error. A rule that keeps
            failing stays as one alert, with a count of how many times it has been seen. Rules that were skipped because
            their conditions didn't hold aren't failures and raise nothing. The alert clears the next time the rule runs
            without errors.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
